AB  - Data on species composition and phenology of a small mammal coenosis on a stream bank in the Niederbergisches Land, (Northrhine-Westphalia) during 25 successive months are presented and discussed. The two non-competitive shrew species Sorex minutus and S. coronatus, the vole Clethrionomys glareolus and the mouse Apodemus sylvaticus are dominant. All other species (Talpa europaea, Neomys fodiens, Arvicola terrestris, Microtus sp. and Micromys minutus) use this habitat only fleetingly. -English summary
