TI  - The emergence of Ephemeroptera, Plecoptera and Trichoptera (Insecta) from the north German lowland Osterau and Rodenbek, two streams of the Late Glacial sands, Schleswig-Holstein
AU  - Speth, S.
T2  - Limnologica
AB  - The emergence of Ephemeroptera, Plecoptera and Trichoptera from two streams was investigated from March to November 1990. A total of 42 species was recorded: 10 species of Ephemeroptera, 7 species of Plecoptera and 25 species of Trichoptera. The highest species richness (31 species) was found in the emergence trap near Glyceria maxima plants. The Plecoptera were the most frequent group in this emergence trap, (2771 ind., 77% of total); the most frequent species was Leuctra fusca (2737 ind., 98.8% of total number of Plecoptera). Results from this study indicate that spatial patterns of emerging nymphs along the bank of a river can be strongly clumped. Emergence periods and temporal emergence patterns of the recorded Ephemeroptera, Plecoptera and Trichoptera are discussed. -from English summary
