TY  - JOUR
TI  - Watercourse development planning for lowland watercourses - from conflict to the establishment of sustainable habitats
AU  - Tent, L.
T2  - Wasser und Boden
AB  - Although wastewater treatment has become increasingly effective, the structure of the receiving waters as a basis for thriving communities has long been neglected. There is an urgent need to revitalise our watercourses by means of a broad approach that takes into account land use and erosion. One way to achieve this is to involve local groups such as farmers, fishermen and nature conservationists in developing watercourse plans. A guideline for headwaters, for instance, is the reestablishment of the characteristic productive salmonid regions. The results are presented in catalogues which can be used by everybody to lend nature a helping hand. While voluntary cooperation is the basis for sustainable effort, the implementation of existing laws should not to be forgotten. Voluntary approaches will only work within a clear framework.
